section(Section title here) #sec1 {

    definition(inner product) #ip {
        A map $\langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle: V \times V \to \mathbb{R}$ that is bilinear, symmetric, and positive definite.
        
    }

    theorem(cauchy-schwarz) #cs {

        for all vectors $u, v$ in an inner product space:
        $$$
        |\langle u, v \rangle| \le \|u\| \|v\|
        $$$

        alternatively, multiline math can be written as:
        mlmath {
            |\langle u, v \rangle| \le \|u\| \|v\|
        }

        and the triple dollar signs alias to the mlmath block 

        proof {
            the proof goes here
            more proof lines
            more
        }

        example {
            this is an example
        }

    }

    subsection(subsection title) #sub1 {

    remark {
        @cs follows from pos def required of @ip
    }

    }
}

section(second section) #sec2 {

    this is an example of inline `code`

    multiline code can be written as:
    ```rust
    some rust code here
    ```

    or:
    code(python) {
        some python code here
    }

    the backticks alias to the code block and both will be syntax highlighted based on the lang

}


